Q58. What is the biggest technical challenge you faced?
Answer

One major challenge was balancing real-time performance with detection accuracy.

Running AI inference on every frame while keeping the desktop application responsive required careful architecture.

Separating detection from the GUI using threads, managing audio playback correctly, and ensuring proper cleanup during shutdown were key challenges that required thoughtful design rather than just writing detection logic.

Q59. If I asked you to improve accuracy by 20%, what would you do?
Answer

I would combine multiple indicators instead of relying only on eye closure:

Mouth opening (yawn detection)
Head pose estimation
Blink frequency over time
Face orientation
Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR)
Temporal smoothing across consecutive frames

Combining these signals would reduce false positives and improve overall robustness compared to using a single feature.

